.TH PDFTOALL 1 "2026-11-13" "pdftoall 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdftoall \- convert PDF into DOCX, XLSX and PPTX locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdftoall convert
[\-o DIR] [\-f docx,pptx,xlsx] [\-e native|docling|marker] [\-\-libreoffice] FILE
.br
.B pdftoall info
FILE
.br
.B pdftoall engines
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdftoall
parses a PDF into an intermediate document model and renders it to Office
formats. No network access is used and no document leaves the machine.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-out\-dir DIR
Where to write the results (default: next to the input file).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-formats LIST
Comma separated targets: docx, pptx, xlsx (default: all three).
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-engine NAME
Parsing engine: native (default), docling, marker.
.TP
.B \-\-libreoffice
Use the experimental LibreOffice PDF-import path (layout fidelity, poor editability).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SH EXAMPLES
pdftoall convert report.pdf -o out/
.br
pdftoall convert report.pdf -f xlsx -e native
.br
pdftoall info report.pdf
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 on a conversion or usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/vkust/PdfToAll
